ne, then down to the river) and the ford three ways (stone by stone, the sung bridge, the run for the far bank). No dice, no Qi for a bridge he doesn't sing: it simply works, and whoever is with him can't fly, so he ferries them. Every other check in the game (singing a ladder down the shaft, the prologue hunts, and the rest) is still rolled at ${realmName(FLY_FROM_REALM)}. <b>Fights:</b> from Act 1 on, never in the prologue, and only at <b>${realmName(FLY_FROM_REALM)}</b> or above: in an armed fight, any round James throws <b>Bone darts</b> or the <b>Qi blast</b> he does it from the air, and that round enemies that don't fly can't reach him: they get no attack on him, though hawks and anything else with wings still do. Blade, spear, flail, needle, guard, the spike field and the Qi shield are done on the ground as before, Yuki is attacked as usual, and none of this applies in a spar or a brawl. While no flying foe is standing, a round from the air in which nobody takes damage (no foe, not James) is a stalemate round: after ${AIR_STALL_WARN} in a row the log warns you, and after ${AIR_STALL_END} in a row the fight is lost, because James's attacks from the air are doing nothing and he has to come down to a foe that is ready for him; any damage on either side starts the count again. <b>The locals</b> can fly the same way, but only from Golden Core, and slower and clumsier. Nobody James has met so far is near that, so expect staring. He doesn't mind.`, 'fly'],
